{"rating":{"source":"Steam","score":88,"max":100,"votes":3333,"summary":"Very Positive"},"reviews":[{"text":"I mean it's alright.\n\n$30? I dunno. It's no SOTN. The real problem with this game, what absolutely kills it, is the exploration. The rewards just aren't worth it. It's always either crafting materials, of which you'll have a near endless supply just by playing without exploration, or it's orange goo which upgrades your character. The thing is, this game isn't difficult. After a couple upgrades, I don't think anybody is going need the additional health pool. The extra stamina is nice but, you know, it's not worth exploring every inch of the map to improve. You can eyeball a lot of the upgrades ","recommended":true,"votesUp":1,"playtimeHours":9,"timestamp":1778380235},{"text":"After a while this game just turns into Rick and Morty, and not in the good way. Constant dark jokes about dark subject matter to get a reaction out of you that aren't even that funny. The gameplay is subpar and the voice you hear constantly gets grating really quickly.\n\nIf I groan at the thought of playing your game something went wrong.","recommended":false,"votesUp":2,"playtimeHours":8,"timestamp":1779019684},{"text":"Jokes are hilarious, gameplay is abyssmal. I can't recommend for the reason that everything just gets samey and the guns don't punch like they could. SFX is very underwhelming.","recommended":false,"votesUp":0,"playtimeHours":3,"timestamp":1780114563}],"players":21}